  ;; The deepseek profiles are the committed default. The provider/model
  ;; comes from the committed .psi/models.edn (deepseek-v4-flash via
  ;; https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic), so the profiles resolve on fresh
  ;; checkouts and in CI — the delegate-review live test mirrors the
  ;; production bootstrap and loads the committed project models file, so
  ;; `bb test` (which snapshots these profiles) stays green. The only
  ;; user-local requirement is the runtime DEEPSEEK_API_KEY env var (the
  ;; auth spec is env:DEEPSEEK_API_KEY). The anthropic and openai maps
  ;; above are alternatives — flip the desired map in/out locally.
  ;;
  ;; NOTE (review 39; adaptive shape VERIFIED live 2026-08-09): these
  ;; profiles plus the committed .psi/models.edn (:adaptive-thinking true)
  ;; activate the adaptive wire shape repo-wide — every delegated workflow
  ;; turn sends thinking.type "adaptive" + output_config.effort. DeepSeek's
  ;; Thinking Mode guide documents only type "enabled"/"disabled" and
  ;; "adaptive" appears nowhere in its Anthropic API docs
  ;; (doc/custom-providers.md's DeepSeek notes; verified 2026-08-07), but
  ;; the task's review-1 live smoke test (2026-08-09, now unblocked) sent
  ;; psi's exact adaptive request (thinking.type "adaptive" +
  ;; output_config.effort "high", x-api-key auth, /v1/messages) and DeepSeek
  ;; returned 200 with a thinking content block — the adaptive shape is
  ;; accepted and thinking runs with the requested effort. The streaming
  ;; 400-retry (:without-thinking) and non-streaming hard-fail asymmetry
  ;; remain as general safety nets for a future rejection; the documented
  ;; fallback is :adaptive-thinking false (classic type: "enabled", a
  ;; documented honored value) — note the committed-file ↔ doc-example
  ;; equality parse-lock
  ;; (committed-project-models-edn-matches-documented-deepseek-example-test
  ;; in user_models_test.clj) means .psi/models.edn and the
  ;; doc/custom-providers.md example must move together if the fallback is
  ;; chosen.
